									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cedar1974" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6965456); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6965456&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609077519" alt="Cedar1974" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6965456)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cedar1974" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6965456); return false;" >Cedar1974</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609075043 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 Dec 2020 13:17</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13899776/possible-keter-class-article-hurricane-omega">Possible Keter Class article Hurricane Omega</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4855002">
									

<blockquote>
<p>&quot;In the event that more than twenty-one named tropical cyclones occur in the Atlantic basin in a season, additional storms will take names from the Greek alphabet.&quot;</p>
<p>24 letters in the Greek alphabet, so that's 21+24 which is 45. 45 tropical cyclones/hurricanes in one hurricane season. That's immensely unrealistic unless it's an XK-Class end-of-the-world scenario.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That's the idea, it is an XK-Class EotW Scenario. But the record itself is what is anomlious.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>So.. this seems like a tale to me. Not an SCP object. It's just a hurricane. They die out after a few weeks or less. An SCP causes a hurricane, the Foundation tries to stop it. That should be a tale. Also, how do you contain a hurricane?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well, I had the idea that the story was found in several glass bottles that look to have been in the ocean for decades, but one is found in the Arizona Desert, one in the Himalayas, One in the Alps, and so on and so on. Basically, they are all found far from any body of water. The information in the bottles tells the story of a Hurricane season so devastating that when Hurricane Omega hits it does not die out, much like the red spot on Jupiter. The fact these bottles are found with the info in them makes no sense because no such event has happened yet, and no one can tell if maybe SCP-2000 activated and fixed the damage or if the bottles came from somewhere else.</p>
<p>And you don't contain a hurricane, you neutralize it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Overall, this idea is interesting but as an SCP it would not work (it's not anomalous). If you can make it out as a tale, that would hopefully work out and be interesting. Also, its never specified if it's a tale or an SCP.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well, the Storm itself could be anomalous as an XK event that maybe the Chaos Insurgency set off and lost control. I am thinking the Foundation built a Special site called the ARK just for such an emergency. I am thinking of making it a tale like the one that goes along with SCP-5000. That is kind of where I got the idea.</p>

							</div>

								
					
