			<div class="content" id="post-content-4854966">
									

<p>Triple-bracket links are superior to single-bracket links and should be used where possible, such as cross-links with other pages on the wiki. As such they are considered allowable formatting edits on pages.</p>
<p>However, it is important to be sure that they are used appropriately. Triple-bracket links with a full URL (e.g. <tt><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">[[[http://www.scpwiki.com/some-page]]]</span></tt>) are no better than single-bracket links, and some kinds of references (most notably forums) cannot be referenced using triple-bracket page name notation (i.e. <tt><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">[[[some-page|Link&#32;label&#32;here]]]</span></tt>.</p>
<p>Provided that you are only editing pages you come across casually, I'm fine with these changes. Please do not seek out large numbers of pages to edit. If you have an extensive list of pages to be changed, please bring it to staff instead.</p>
<p>Also note that staff reserves the right to issue cease-and-desist orders for any edits being carried out in an improper manner.</p>

